## TASK

Produce ONE consolidated output for {{ layer_name }} that:

1) Preserves the same overall section structure and field layout used by the
   probes. Downstream F-phase processing reads the same field names; do not
   rename or restructure fields.

2) Includes every distinct lexical item, opposition, construction, group,
   pattern, or evidential observation that appears in any probe. Deduplicate
   strictly: two items count as the same only when they share the same
   surface form (with the same script/transliteration). Near-synonyms or
   morphologically related items are SEPARATE entries.

3) For each item, preserve the original [CORE] / [MARGINAL] / [UNCERTAIN] tag
   (or whatever epistemic-status convention the probes used). When the same
   item appears in multiple probes with conflicting tags, keep the **most
   conservative** tag (UNCERTAIN > MARGINAL > CORE).

4) When two probes give different usage descriptions for the same item,
   keep the more specific / better-evidenced description. Cite the union of
   contexts attested across probes (e.g., if probe 1 cites a legal context
   and probe 2 cites an aesthetic context, the merged entry mentions both).

5) For prose-style probes (P2/P3/P4 commentary), preserve all distinct
   observations as separate paragraphs or bullets. Do NOT synthesize a new
   overarching narrative — the merged output is an inventory, not a
   re-analysis.

## HARD RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

R1) **NO NEW FORMS.** Never include a form, opposition, or construction that
    does not appear verbatim in at least one probe.

R2) **NO INVENTED EXAMPLES.** Cite only example sentences that appear in the
    probes. Do not paraphrase examples; quote them as given.

R3) **NO TAG INFLATION.** If a probe tags an item [MARGINAL] and another tags
    it [CORE], the merged tag is [MARGINAL]. Do not promote items.

R4) **NO META-COMMENTARY.** Do not add notes like "this item appeared in 2
    of 3 probes" or "probes agreed on X". The output should look like a
    single CLCA P-phase output for {{ layer_name }}, not a meta-comparison
    of probes.

R5) **PRESERVE FORMAT EXACTLY.** Use the same markdown conventions
    (heading style, bold-vs-numbered list, field labels) that the probes
    use. F-phase extractors depend on this consistency.

